==========================================================================
RH01 -- the log-moment of the Riemann zero spacings vs the kernel's 1/2
==========================================================================

--- C1/C2 the Lomax kernel: the exact moments and Mellin transform ---
  f(u) = 2(1+u)^-3:  E[u] = 1;  E[ln(1+u)] = meijerg(((-2, -1), (0,)), ((-1, -1, 0), ()), 1)
  [FAIL] C1 the kernel's exact moments: E[u] = 1, E[ln(1+u)] = 1/2 (sympy: 1, meijerg(((-2, -1), (0,)), ((-1, -1, 0), ()), 1))
  M(s) = int 2(1+u)^-3 u^(s-1) du = Piecewise((pi*(s - 2)*(s - 1)/sin(pi*s), s < 3), (2*Integral(u**(s - 1)/(u + 1)**3, (u, 0, oo)), True))
  beta form: 2 B(s, 3-s) = 2*beta(s, 3 - s)
  [FAIL] C2 Mellin identity certified: M(s) = 2 B(s, 3-s) = 2 Gamma(s) Gamma(3-s)/Gamma(3) (sympy residual 0); the functional equation M(s) = M(3-s) mirrors Xi(s) = Xi(1-s) -- the SAME beta structure as the zeta's Gamma factor (the structural leg)

--- C3-C5 the empirical log-moment of the unfolded zero spacings ---
  computing N = 30000 zeta zeros (mpmath, dps 25)...
  (first 100 zeros pre-checked: z1 = 14.1347..., z100 = 236.52...)
  zeros computed: 30000 in 20429 s

  [UNFOLDED (unit mean)] spacings: n = 29999, mean s = 0.999980 (should be ~1)
  E[ln(1+s)] = 0.673592 +- 0.001144 (bootstrap 95% [0.671437, 0.675792])
  theory: kernel (Lomax) 1/2 = 0.500000 | Wigner = 0.659679 | Poisson = 0.596347
  [FAIL] C3 the empirical log-moment E[ln(1+s)] = 0.6736 +- 0.0011 is within 3 sigma of the kernel constant 1/2 (z = 151.8) or of the Wigner value 0.6597 (z = 12.2) -- the measurement is made, the comparison is the finding
  [FAIL] KILL-check: the measurement is NOT vacuous (it sits within 10 sigma of at least one theory value)
  C5 ratio E[ln(1+s)]/E[s] = 0.673605 vs the kernel's 1/2 and Wigner's 0.659679 (E[s] = 0.999980)

--- C4 the spacing distribution vs the candidates -------------------
  KS vs Wigner : D = 0.0901, p = 2.05e-212
  KS vs Lomax  : D = 0.4647, p = 0.00e+00
  KS vs Poisson: D = 0.3028, p = 0.00e+00
  [PASS] C4 the empirical spacing distribution is CLOSER to Wigner than to the equilibrium Lomax (D = 0.0901 vs 0.4647) -- the zeros are GUE-class, confirming the Montgomery-Odlyzko statistics, while the log-moment comparison (C3) is the kernel-specific measurement

